    "title": "What channel is Iowa vs Nebraska basketball today? Time, TV schedule to watch Sweet 16 game",
    "text": "March 26, 2026, 5:47 p.m. ETAre you ready for some corn-ball?Were it not for the Sweet 16 moniker for their March Madness meeting, that might be an apt name for the rubber match between No. 4 seed Nebraska and No. 9 seed Iowa. The winner of the all-Big Ten basketball meeting on Thursday, March 26 will advance to play in the Elite Eight.It would be Iowa's first such berth since 1987, and Nebraska's first, ever.Stream select March Madness games live with Sling TVStorylines abound for the meeting between the Cornhuskers and Hawkeyes, not least of which is both teams have split their regular-season meetings. Iowa took the first meeting on Feb. 17, 56-52, while Nebraska returned the favor on March 8 with an 85-74 overtime win.Nebraska, of course, is delving further into the Men's NCAA Tournament than ever before, notching their first two victories in program history with wins over No. 13-seed Troy and No. 5-seed Vanderbilt. iowa advanced to the Sweet 16 with a technical first-round upset over No. 8 seed Clemson in the first round; no qualifier is necessary for the second upset, however, with the Hawkeyes knocking out defending national champion and No. 1 seed Florida with a buzzer-beating 3 from Alvaro Folgueiras.Here's how to watch the all-Big Ten Sweet 16 matchup between Iowa and Nebraska, including game time, TV and streaming information, game odds and more:What channel is Iowa vs Nebraska basketball on today in Sweet 16?TV: TBS/truTVStreaming: NCAA March Madness Live | Sling TVIowa and Nebraska's Sweet 16 game will simulcast nationally on TBS and truTV, with Kevin Harlan, Robbie Hummel, Stan Van Gundy and Lauren Shehadi on the call. Streaming options for the game include NCAA March Madness Live on the NCAA's website (with a valid cable login) and Sling TV, which covers both TBS and truTV.Stream Iowa-Nebraska live with Sling TVIowa-Nebraska Sweet 16 game time todayDate: Thursday March 26Time: 7:30 p.m. ET | 6:30 p.m. CTLocation: Toyota Center (Houston)Iowa and Nebraska's Sweet 16 game is scheduled to tip off at 7:30 p.m. ET (6:30 p.m. CT) on March 26 from the Toyota Center in Houston.Iowa vs Nebraska picks, predictions, odds in Sweet 16Odds courtesy of BetMGM as of 5 p.m. ET on March 26Odds: Nebraska (-1.5)Over/under: 132.5Moneyline: Nebraska -130 | Iowa +110PredictionsJohn Leuzzi: NebraskaJordan Mendoza: NebraskaEhsan Kassim: NebraskaAustin Curtright: IowaOur team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.Gambling involves risk. Please only gamble with funds that you can comfortably afford to lose. While we do our utmost to offer good advice and information we cannot be held responsible for any loss that may be incurred as a result of gambling. We do our best to make sure all the information that we provide on this site is correct. However, from time to time mistakes will be made and we will not be held liable. Please check any stats or information if you are unsure how accurate they are. No guarantees are made with regards to results or financial gain. All forms of betting carry financial risk and it is up to the individual to make bets with or without the assistance of information provided on this site and we cannot be held responsible for any loss that may be incurred as a result of following the betting tips provided on this site. Past performances do not guarantee success in the future and betting odds fluctuate from one minute to the next. The material contained on this site is intended to inform, entertain and educate the reader and in no way represents an inducement to gamble legally or illegally or any sort of professional advice.Gannett may earn revenue from sports betting operators for audience referrals to betting services. Sports betting operators have no influence over nor are any such revenues in any way dependent on or linked to the newsro